{% extends '@ExactApproval/base.html.twig' %}
{% block title %}Alert policy · Verified Human Approval{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
<p class="eyebrow">Administrator · Riverside Council</p><h1>Who can issue public alerts</h1>
<p>An evacuation order is a high-stakes change. Many people can be allowed to issue one, as long as the roles you choose must verify each exact alert with their own passkey. The application enforces this rule itself, whether the request comes from this site, an AI agent over MCP or any other client.</p>
{% if saved %}<p class="notice">Policy saved. Requests waiting under the old rules can no longer be approved.</p>{% endif %}
<section class="card">{{ form_start(form) }}{{ form_widget(form) }}<p class="muted">Read-only colleagues cannot issue alerts. Placeholders for the statement: {% verbatim %}{{title}}, {{revision}}, {{application}}, {{environment}}{% endverbatim %}.</p><button>Save policy</button>{{ form_end(form) }}</section>
<section class="card"><h2>What the approver confirms</h2><p class="statement">{{ preview }}</p></section>
{% endblock %}
